/**
 * Natur & geografi → Ekologi & miljö → Föroreningar & avfall, 2931–2937 (0.46): air, water and soil pollution,
 * plastic and microplastic, chemical waste, source sorting and recycling, and environmental toxins.
 * Recurring signs: pollution is drawn as brown-grey puffs, brown water or a dark stain; poison and toxic
 * substances are small purple dots or a purple drop; clean things are blue and green. The thing the word names is
 * coloured and ringed in orange, while the rest is pale or grey. Abstract words are small symbolic scenes where the
 * coloured idea dominates and a grey copy stands beside it as contrast. Warning signs follow the general hazard
 * pictogram shape (a red-edged diamond) without any text. No words, no letters, no brands and no pointing fingers.
 */
